# Templates & Frontend

## Layout
- `base.html` — shared layout: navbar, Bootstrap 5.3 CDN, Bootstrap Icons 1.11, HTMX 1.9.10
- All pages `{% extends "base.html" %}` and fill `{% block content %}`, `{% block extra_css %}`, `{% block extra_js %}`

## HTMX Usage Pattern
The dashboard filter form uses HTMX:
```html
<form hx-post="/dashboard/filter" hx-target="#questionList" hx-indicator="#loading">
```
The server detects `HX-Request` header and returns only the `partials/question_list.html` fragment.

**Rule**: All new HTMX interactions should target a specific `id` container and return the matching partial template. Full-page fallback is also supported by checking for the HTMX header.

## Shared Partials
| File | Used by |
|---|---|
| `partials/question_list.html` | Dashboard (HTMX target), admin questions list |
| `partials/edit_question_modal.html` | Dashboard + admin `Question Management` — shared 3-tab Edit modal markup + `#renameConfirmModal` + `#mdEditorModal` + `#toastContainer` + edit-modal-scoped CSS |
| `partials/edit_question_modal_js.html` | Same hosts — bundles the entire Edit-modal JS (open / save / rename / asset upload / MD editor / paste handler) AND pulls in `partials/tag_editor_js.html`, so do NOT include `tag_editor_js.html` separately on the host |
| `partials/tag_editor_form.html` | Tags tab of the shared Edit modal (above), admin Add-question wizard Step 3 (borrowed via JS DOM move) |
| `partials/tag_editor_js.html` | Loaded transitively by `edit_question_modal_js.html`. Do not include separately. |
| `partials/md_editor.html` | Loaded transitively by `edit_question_modal.html` (idempotent); also used by the fullscreen `admin_md_editor.html` |

## Multi-Select Dropdowns (custom, not native `<select multiple>`)
Topics, subtopics, chapters, years all use a custom dropdown pattern:
- Bootstrap dropdown component with `data-bs-auto-close="outside"`
- Checkboxes inside the dropdown panel
- A hidden `<select multiple>` stores the selected values for form submission
- Search input inside each dropdown for filtering options
- "All" / "None" quick-select buttons

When adding a new multi-select filter, follow the same pattern for consistency.

## SSE (Server-Sent Events)
Used for ingestion, health sync, batch IMG generation, and batch MCQ ANS assignment. All streaming endpoints follow the same event shape:

```javascript
const es = new EventSource('/admin/questions/batch-mcq-ans?' + params);
es.onmessage = e => {
    const ev = JSON.parse(e.data);
    // ev.type: 'info' | 'success' | 'skip' | 'error' | 'done'
    // ev.message: human-readable string
    // ev.current / ev.total: optional progress counters
    appendLog(ev.message, ev.type);
    if (ev.type === 'done') es.close();
};
```
The server yields `data: {...}\n\n` using Flask `Response(generate(), mimetype='text/event-stream', headers={'Cache-Control': 'no-cache', 'X-Accel-Buffering': 'no'})`.

nginx must have `proxy_buffering off` for SSE to work through a reverse proxy.

## Generation Status Polling
`generate.html` polls `GET /generate/status/<id>` every 2 seconds until `status` is `completed` or `failed`, then shows a download link.

## My Files Auto-Refresh
`my_files.html` runs `setInterval` every 5 seconds, but only re-fetches if any row has the `.status-generating` class.

## Shared JS helpers in `base.html`

The base template defines a set of global helpers that every preview / asset interaction in the app reuses. Don't duplicate this logic per-page.

| Helper | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `window.oqbTypesetMath(root)` | Typeset KaTeX math inside `root`. Called after Markdown inserts. |
| `window.oqbRenderMarkdownInto(el, html)` | Set inner HTML + auto-typeset math. |
| `window.oqbLoadMarkdownPreviewCards(root)` | Lazy-loads `.md-preview-card[data-preview-q]` placeholders by hitting `/dashboard/api/question/<id>/preview/<type>`. Branches on `mode` (image / html / thumbnail / download) and uses `_oqbBuildThumbHtml` for the DOC `thumbnail` shape. |
| `window.oqbPollDocThumbnails(root)` | Polls `data-doc-pending-id` elements every 3 s (×60 attempts ≈ 3 min). Uses the SAME cache-busted URL for both the `Image()` probe and the swap-in `<img src>` so the rerender button immediately picks up the new PNG. Per-element dedup via `data-doc-poller-active`. |
| `window.oqbRerenderThumb(qid, aid, btn)` | POSTs to `/admin/questions/<qid>/assets/<aid>/rerender-thumb`, then re-arms the placeholder for the poller. Admin-only — gated on `window.OQB_IS_ADMIN`. |
| `_oqbBuildThumbHtml(url, filename, dl, aid, qid)` | Builds the inner HTML for a DOC thumbnail (image + filename + download + admin rerender button). Used by both the live poller swap and `oqbLoadMarkdownPreviewCards`. |
| `window.OQB_IS_ADMIN` | Boolean emitted by Jinja in `base.html` — true when the user has any subject-admin or super-admin role. Used to gate admin-only UI like the per-preview rerender button. |

`oqbLoadMarkdownPreviewCards` and `oqbPollDocThumbnails` auto-run on `DOMContentLoaded` AND on every `htmx:afterSwap` event, so HTMX-driven dashboard refreshes pick up new placeholders without bespoke wiring.

**`viewer.html` does NOT extend `base.html`** — it has its own minimal copies of `oqbTypesetMath` and `oqbRenderMarkdownInto`. When adding a new shared helper, decide whether the viewer needs it; if so, duplicate it inline. The rerender button is intentionally NOT exposed in the viewer because forking that helper there would add too much code for the use case.

## Question Edit Modal Tabs (shared)
The `#editQuestionModal` markup lives in `partials/edit_question_modal.html` and is mounted by BOTH `dashboard.html` (admin-gated) and `admin_questions.html`. Tab order is fixed at:
1. **Tags** (default active) — borrows `partials/tag_editor_form.html`; the admin Add-question wizard temporarily relocates this `<form id="editForm">` into its Step 3 area via `borrowTagFormForAdd()` / `returnTagFormToEditModal()`.
2. **Assets** — upload / delete / reorder per language (EN / CH / BI) and per asset type (QUE / ANS / SOL). Supports IMG (multi-part), MD (single-slot, inline editor via `#mdEditorModal`), DOC (single-slot upload + download).
3. **Details** — QID rename (via `#renameConfirmModal`) + read-only `created_at`.

`openEditModal(questionId)` is the entry point — it fetches `GET /admin/questions/<id>/details` and `GET /admin/questions/<id>/assets`, populates the tag form via the shared `populateTagForm`, and shows the modal.

**Refresh callback contract**: the modal's save / rename / asset flows call `window.oqbAfterQuestionEdit?.()` after a successful mutation. Each host page wires its own implementation immediately after the include:

```js
window.oqbAfterQuestionEdit = loadQuestions;       // admin questions page
window.oqbAfterQuestionEdit = refreshCurrentPage;  // dashboard
```

The admin **Add Question** modal keeps its own Details → Assets → Tags 3-step wizard (Step 1 must create the question record before assets/tags can attach to it) — only the Edit modal is unified across pages.

**localStorage keys used by the Edit modal:**
- `oqb_assetThumbsCompact` — `'1'` | `'0'`: compact vs full-width asset preview mode. Applied as a `<body>.asset-thumbs-compact` class via `oqbInitThumbCompact()` in `edit_question_modal_js.html`.

## Drag-to-Reorder
Sort criteria (dashboard + generate page) and the generator's Selected Questions list use **SortableJS** (loaded from CDN in `base.html`). HTML5 native drag-and-drop is **not** used — it does not work on touch devices.

Standard config used by all sortable lists in this project:
```js
Sortable.create(container, {
    handle: '.drag-handle',
    animation: 150,
    ghostClass: 'sortable-ghost',
    chosenClass: 'sortable-chosen',
    dragClass: 'sortable-drag',
    forceFallback: true,        // unified mouse + touch path
    fallbackTolerance: 4,
    delay: 100,
    delayOnTouchOnly: true,
    touchStartThreshold: 4,
    onEnd(evt) { /* reorder model array using evt.oldIndex / evt.newIndex */ }
});
```
Init is idempotent — stash the instance on `container._sortableInstance` and bail if already set, so re-rendering children doesn't double-init.

The `.drag-handle` element needs `touch-action: none` (already set globally in `base.html`) so the browser doesn't steal the touch for scrolling. Bigger handle hit area on coarse-pointer / mobile is also defined globally.
